### Test results
- `python -m pytest tests` → 170 passed (33 new; 137 → 170).
- Coverage (`--cov=anvil_runtime`): 94% overall. New modules: model_router 100%,
  openhands_adapter 100%, session_bridge 100%, tool_authorizer 100%, core_tools 100%,
  openrouter_provider 100%, usage_tracker 98%, mcp_cache 94%, mcp_manager 93%,
  skills resolver/loader/manifest 82/84/78% (overall ≥70% met).

### Design decisions (within blueprint/spec, no drift)
- All external integrations are behind injected interfaces with deterministic
  offline defaults: MCP `ServerConnector` (default EmptyConnector), OpenRouter
  `CompletionTransport` (default OfflineTransport), OpenHands `OpenHandsBackend`
  (default InProcessBackend). This satisfies the architecture "in-process now,
  transport-agnostic later" note and keeps the runtime + tests network-free with
  no hard dependency on the openhands package.
- Model slugs follow the policy-example convention (`deepseek-coder`, spec §4.3);
  `gemma-4` is the planning/analysis slug. `_CODING_PHASES = {implementation, qa}`
  default to the coding model; all others default to the planning model; review
  inherits the phase default (architecture §305).
- ModelRouter.select() reuses the Slice 3 PolicyEngine.enforce() so model-allowlist
  remediation (switch-to-allowed-model) is shared, not reimplemented.
- Helper contracts (MCPServer, DiscoveredTool, ToolInvocationRequest/Result,
  SkillRef/SkillBundle, CompletionRequest/Response, AgentRuntimeConfig/PhaseStep/
  StepResult, PhaseUsage, ModelRouteDecision) live inside their assigned matrix
  modules — no new module files (same approach as Slices 2/3/4).

### Issues encountered and fixes
- openrouter_provider initially at 0% line coverage (no required test referenced it).
  Added tests/unit/runtime/test_openrouter_provider.py → 100%. No functional change.
- All suites passed on the first full run after authoring; no retries needed.

### Drift check (against blueprint / architecture / spec)
- Modules created == the Slice-5 rows of the plan §8 assignment matrix
  (tools/{mcp_manager,mcp_cache,core_tools,tool_authorizer}; skills/{loader,resolver,
  manifest}; llm/{openrouter_provider,model_router,usage_tracker}; sdk/{openhands_adapter,
  session_bridge}). No unmapped source modules; package __init__.py are scaffolding.
- No Slice 1 protected files and no Slice 2 modules (development_manager, phase
