### Test results
- `python -m pytest tests` → 208 passed (38 new; 170 → 208).
- Coverage (`--cov=anvil_runtime`): 94% overall. Slice 6: validator 99%, drift
  checker 98%, classifier 94%, remediation 100%, redaction 96%, specialist_registry
  91%, metadata 90%, event_bus 93%. Plan §4 per-package targets met (core ≈93%,
  policy ≈92%, state ≈88%, api ≈98%; all ≥ their thresholds; overall ≥70%).

### Design decisions (within blueprint/spec, no drift)
- Artifact validation is deterministic pass/fail (FR-AR-002): required-section
  checks scan heading lines only, so body prose mentioning a section word cannot
  mask a missing heading.
- Drift checker emits findings strictly in Blueprint→Architecture→Spec order
  (FR-DR-002A) and classifies each via the shared classifier; remediation routing
  is a pure function of (highest severity, attempt) with a 2-attempt budget.
- Redaction is centralized in the EventBus write path (the spec's "redaction applied
  before logging"); the optional redactor keeps every prior test green while making
  secret-free audit trails the default for hardened runs.
- Specialist registry is fail-safe: invalid roles are dropped at load with a
  SpecialistRoleRejected audit event, an absent registry yields an empty model
  (backward-compatible), and protected-path/phase bounds are enforced at both
  validation and invocation.
- Helper models live inside their assigned matrix modules — no new module files.

### Issues encountered and fixes
- Three test-side issues surfaced on the first full run (no implementation defects):
  (1) a redaction assertion checked a substring of the *label* not the value;
  (2) the artifact "missing section" test left the section word in body prose —
  fixed by tightening the validator to check heading lines only (a real
  improvement); (3) the drift-rollback e2e called rollback() directly, which does
  not resume the run — switched to the real apply_override(rollback) path that
  resets status to running. All green after fixes (208 passed).

### Drift check (against blueprint / architecture / spec)
- Modules created == the Slice-6 rows of the plan §8 assignment matrix
  (artifacts/{validator,schemas,metadata}; drift/{checker,classifier,remediation};
  agents/specialist_registry; security/redaction). state/event_bus.py is the matrix
  "Slices 2 and 6" row — modified here for the planned redaction/completeness pass.
- No protected shared contract files (phase_contracts.py, api/models.py,
  config/schema.py) were modified. No unmapped modules. No drift detected.

